y, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, etc.\n\nCandidate B seems strong on conscientiousness (reliability), stress handling, weather assessment (technical), but has communication tone issues and pretentiousness (cooperation). Candidate D has problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner (cooperation). Candidate A has anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but unfriendly and unhealthy (maybe reliability). Candidate C makes quick correct decisions, excellent attention, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (development), but puts concern for others above everything (cooperation?).\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps propose Candidate B as leading, but note concerns. Or propose Candidate D? Let's weigh.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well. D responds adequately to unexpected events (maybe less strong). A not mentioned stress. C quick decisions maybe under pressure.\n\nReliability: B very conscientious. D takes responsibility seriously. A unfriendly, unhealthy (maybe reliability concerns). C not willing to further education (maybe less development).\n\nCooperation: A unfriendly, B pretentious and wrong tone, C difficulty communicating, egocentric, D loner, moody.\n\nAll have cooperation concerns. Which is least? C puts concern for others above everything, maybe good cooperation despite communication difficulty. D loner/moody maybe worse. B pretentious maybe moderate. A unfriendly.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership (maybe cockpit). B good at weather, computer skills. C quick decisions, attention. D problem solving, concentration.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions. A anticipates dangerous situations (good). D adequate response.\n\nOverall, maybe Candidate B balances reliability and stress, but communication issues. Candidate C strong decision and attention, but egocentric and not willing to further education. Might be risk.\n\nI think start by recommending Candidate B, but note concerns about communication tone. Provide evidence. Also ask other panel members about any additional observations on Candidate B's cooperation.\n\nWe need to include vote in metadata. So vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
